1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lustick, Evelyn M. (nee Nemanich) At rest on December 28, 2011.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survived by her two sons David F. (Marjorie) and Calvin F. (Bettie) Lustick; grandchildren David Lustick, Jeffrey (Chris) Lustick and Melyssa (Alex) Markin; Angi (Rich) Babicki and Kimberley Lustick; great-grandchildren Alan, Kyle
2 CONC , Amelia and Jakob; Jacob, Amber and Ryan; brother Norman (late Marilyn) Nemanich. Also survived by numerous nieces, nephews, cousins and friends.
2 CONT
2 CONT Preceded in death by her daughter Clarice E. Lustick; husband Frank J. Lustick; parents John and Mary (nee Simonich) Nemanich; brother John (late Clarice) Nemanich; sister Dorothy (Jerry) Horvat.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lifetime member of St. Joseph Church, former president of the Rosarians; Altar and Rosary Society, St. Joseph Seniors, Slovenian Women's Union Branch 20, KSKJ St. Francis Society. Evelyn was also a volunteer at Shepherd's Table. S
2 CONC he enjoyed bowling, Bingo and was a lifelong Chicago White Sox fan. Above all, a Sacristan for many years at St. Joseph Church and reciting the rosary at four o'clock Mass, was her greatest joy.
2 CONT
2 CONT In lieu of flowers, memorial contributions in Evelyn's name to St. Joseph Church or to St. Joseph Academy would be appreciated.
2 CONT
2 CONT A special thanks to the residents and staff at Our Lady of Angels Retirement Home.
2 CONT
2 CONT A Celebration of Evelyn's life will begin on Wednesday, January 4, 2012, at 9:30 am with prayers at the funeral home chapel, then in procession to St. Joseph Church, Joliet for a Mass of Christian Burial at 10:00 am. Interment to 
2 CONC follow at St. Joseph Cemetery, Joliet. Visitation will be on Tuesday from 2:00 to 7:00 pm at:
2 CONT
2 CONT
