1 NOTE {geni:about_me} JoAnn Dyck passed away March 15th, 2014 at Banner Hospice Medical Center of Respiratory failure. JoAnn was born on February 5th, 1930 in Butte, MT to Josephine Sink and Jack Hamilton. She moved to Bozeman, MT and t
2 CONC hen on to Renton, WA where she finished her schooling. She married Julius Baker and had a son, Michael. She later married Arthur Dyck and they had a son, Douglas. Both Art and Doug preceded JoAnn in death. They lived in Las Vegas,
2 CONC  NV where they both taught school JoAnn became a counselor at Basic High School in Henderson, NV. Upon retiring they moved to Squim, WA where they built a new home. After leaving WA they moved to Sun City West. They enjoyed travel
2 CONC ing and went on numerous cruises. JoAnn loved the theater, she was an avid reader and the sport she enjoyed the most was her bowling leagues. She was an avid sports fan as she always had 2 season tickets behind home plate for the 
2 CONC Seattle Mariners. She was also an enthusiastic Diamondback fan. She was a volunteer weekly for seven years at the two gift shops at Del Webb Hospital.  She is survived by her son, Michael. JoAnn will be missed by all of her many f
2 CONC riends and relatives. Visit this person's Guest Book at www.yourwestvalley.com
