2 DATE 7 AUG 1933
2 ADDR
3 CITY Butte
3 STAE MT
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 28 JUN 2006
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Geraldine (Gerry) Pochervina Benjamin, 72, died Wednesday, June 28, 2006, in Crest Nursing Home, after a long and courageous battle with cancer.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born, in Butte, on Aug. 7, 1933, to John and Theresa (VanNuland) Pochervina. She attended Longfellow Grade School and graduated from Butte High School in 1950.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gerry married Robert "Bob" Benjamin on June 22, 1952, they resided in Butte. Gerry worked in the credit department of Sears until its closure, then went to work for Finnegan Electric, until its closure. She then worked for the hot
2 CONC  lunch program at Butte High School, the after school day care program at Butte Central Elementary, and the concessions at the Civic Center, until her illness forced her to retire. She loved to knit and crochet and cook large fami
2 CONC ly dinners. Almost everyone in the family and many friends have either a sweater knitted by her or a baby blanket crocheted by her. She was always there if anyone needed anything. She enjoyed attending her grandchildren's sporting
2 CONC  events; she was their greatest fan and critic. She loved watching sporting events of all kinds, especially golf and football.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gerry was preceded in death by her parents; sister, Audrey Roberts; brother, Gilbert Pochervina; in-laws, Hubert and Alice Benjamin; husband, Robert; daughter, Patricia Ann; brother-in-law, Jack Benjamin; and niece, Karen Fitzpatr
2 CONC ick.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is survived by her daughter and son-in-law, Terry and Mike Hovan; granddaughters, Meghan, Molly and Mari Hovan; son and daughter-in-law, Bud and Nina Benjamin; grandsons, Cory and Chad Benjamin; brother-in-law, Bill Roberts; s
2 CONC ister-in-law, Frances Benjamin; brothers and sisters-in-law, William and Irene Benjamin, Lynn and Alan Aniksdal, Janice and Pat Fitzpatrick, Sandy and Bill Banfield; numerous nieces, nephews, and cousins, great-nieces, great-nephe
2 CONC ws; two great-great-nieces; one great-great-nephew; and special cousin and friend, Mary Ellen Moe.
2 CONT
2 CONT Liturgy of the Resurrection will be celebrated at 10 a.m. Wednesday in St. John the Evangelist Catholic Church, located on Majors Ave. Interment of Ashes will follow in Holy Cross Catholic Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT In lieu of flowers, the family requests that memorials be made to Highlands Hospice, Our Lady of the Rockies, Butte Catholic Education Fund or donor's choice.
2 CONT
2 CONT Express condolences at www.mtstandard.com/obits.
